{"term":"friction","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:83e657ed58e853f502","definition":"The rubbing of one object or surface against another.","example":"Energy has seldom been found where we need it when we want it. Ancient nomads, wishing to ward off the evening chill and enjoy a meal around a campfire, had to collect wood and then spend time and effort coaxing the heat of friction out from between sticks to kindle a flame.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"usually","register":"uncountable, usually","wordFamily":["antifriction","coefficient of friction","Darcy friction factor","dynamic friction","frictional","frictionally","friction burn","friction clutch","friction drum","friction hitch","frictionite","frictionize","frictionless","friction match","friction pile","frictionproof","friction tape","frictiony","iliotibial band friction syndrome","interfriction","kinetic friction","nanofriction","nonfriction","static friction","sticktion","stiction","underfriction"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/friction#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5c398815880c391bc1","definition":"A force that resists the relative motion or tendency to such motion of two bodies in contact.","example":"Secondly, When a body is once in motion it will continue to move forever, unless something stops it. When a ball is struck on the surface of the earth, the friction of the earth and the resistance of the air soon stop its motion.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"usually","register":"uncountable, usually","wordFamily":["antifriction","coefficient of friction","Darcy friction factor","dynamic friction","frictional","frictionally","friction burn","friction clutch","friction drum","friction hitch","frictionite","frictionize","frictionless","friction match","friction pile","frictionproof","friction tape","frictiony","iliotibial band friction syndrome","interfriction","kinetic friction","nanofriction","nonfriction","static friction","sticktion","stiction","underfriction"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/friction#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:9d589c28c7b4bfdbe1","definition":"A massage of the body to restore circulation.","example":"The frictions should at first be very gentle, and performed with a view to restore heat, and not to force the blood towards the heart, which in drowned persons is already too much distended with it.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete, usually","register":"countable, obsolete, usually","wordFamily":["antifriction","coefficient of friction","Darcy friction factor","dynamic friction","frictional","frictionally","friction burn","friction clutch","friction drum","friction hitch","frictionite","frictionize","frictionless","friction match","friction pile","frictionproof","friction tape","frictiony","iliotibial band friction syndrome","interfriction","kinetic friction","nanofriction","nonfriction","static friction","sticktion","stiction","underfriction"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/friction#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a2dff25e8806dcbb78","definition":"Conflict, as between persons having dissimilar ideas or interests; clash.","example":"Thais have been watching for signs of friction between the armed forces and the monarchy—the country's two biggest sources of political power—since the death in October of Bhumibol Adulyadej, King Vajiralongkorn's long-reigning father.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively, usually","register":"figuratively, uncountable, usually","wordFamily":["antifriction","coefficient of friction","Darcy friction factor","dynamic friction","frictional","frictionally","friction burn","friction clutch","friction drum","friction hitch","frictionite","frictionize","frictionless","friction match","friction pile","frictionproof","friction tape","frictiony","iliotibial band friction syndrome","interfriction","kinetic friction","nanofriction","nonfriction","static friction","sticktion","stiction","underfriction"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/friction#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ccef966ea2961810d6","definition":"Any obstacle or hindrance that makes a system less convenient or desirable to use.","example":"Users have reported friction from having to enter their passwords many times a day.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"usually","register":"uncountable, usually","wordFamily":["antifriction","coefficient of friction","Darcy friction factor","dynamic friction","frictional","frictionally","friction burn","friction clutch","friction drum","friction hitch","frictionite","frictionize","frictionless","friction match","friction pile","frictionproof","friction tape","frictiony","iliotibial band friction syndrome","interfriction","kinetic friction","nanofriction","nonfriction","static friction","sticktion","stiction","underfriction"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/friction#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:de015dd94425077bfe","definition":"Conflict during the Second Sino-Japanese War, as between the Communists and non-hanjian Kuomintang forces.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"China, historical, usually","register":"China, historical, uncountable, usually","wordFamily":["antifriction","coefficient of friction","Darcy friction factor","dynamic friction","frictional",